  ('zcrm_1579374000163575023', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000142011002', 'Jonathan Chan', NULL, '4/21/25: Jenny Chan emailed in asking what plan she''s on and the following:
for future reference.  i''ve been avoiding getting labs doing or seeing my doctor because i don''t know how much i''ll get charged for everything.  can you give me an estimate?
If i went to see Dr Matthew Smith for a regular sick visit or regular routine visit
and how much it will be if i got a full thyroid panel? 

Response: 
Good morning Jenny,
 
You''re currently on the Secure HSA plan with a $5,000 IUA.
 
Unfortunately, I can’t provide an exact estimate for your doctor visit since pricing can vary by provider and location.
 
If you''re going for an annual preventive wellness checkup with an in-network provider, and the doctor orders preventive labs during that visit, your MEC (Minimum Essential Coverage) should cover it at 100%. To confirm if your provider is in-network, you can search the “PHCS Specific Services” network here:https://providersearch.multiplan.com/
 
If the visit is diagnostic (not preventive), I recommend calling the provider’s office directly to ask about their cash-pay rate. For diagnostic labs, we’d be happy to help! Once you have your lab order from the doctor, just fill out our quote request form here: https://mpb.health/request-rx-quote/
We''ll search for the best available pricing on labs, imaging, and prescriptions.
 
If you''re specifically looking for thyroid panel pricing, here are a few examples from our discount lab resources: TSH: $10, T4: $10, T3 Total: $20
If you can provide the full list of tests your doctor ordered, I can send back a more complete quote plus instructions on how to order. 
