  ('zcrm_1579374000163401063', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000011740100', 'Rossana Johnston', NULL, 'Rossana texted me saying the following:
Adam, I just talked to Carent labs. (The provider''s lab choice). The provider sent a letter with explanation and new codes so that the lab reprocess the bill and send that to Planstin. Unfortunately the lab has not received anything. Or has not been entered in their system. The lab lady said there are three steps needed.
1) The lab registers the new info from provider
2) the lab re-process the service items and ands to Planstin.
3) Planstin decides what to reimburse to the lab.
At least 30 days. Both for my and my husbands outstanding invoices with the lab.

I am leaving on Sunday and will be back in July. I can not respond to texts from you as it costs me 1.25 to do. But you can reach my by email or by WhatsApp at my phone number. I will be 7 hrs ahead of the USA.

Thanks

Now the ball is in the labs court and as the message says we have at least 30 days for all of this to be resolved.

AJ', 'Adam Jordano', 'Adam Jordano', '2025-04-17 12:18:42', '2025-04-17 12:18:53'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000163394121', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000077918128', 'Kimber Eastman', NULL, '4/17/25: Kimber called. She presented her planstin card at derm visit. just had a prev skin cancer check and had to pay $400 for the visit. I recommended she call and get a superbill. She can send it to us or ARM for reimbursement. Also requested another physical arm card through portal and provided link to HW app via email and educated her on some of the changes. AM', 'Concierge', 'Concierge', '2025-04-17 11:58:27', '2025-04-17 11:58:27'),
