  ('zcrm_1579374000163360264', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000044118411', 'Nathalie Joly', NULL, '4-16-25 Nathalie called bc Sedera didn''t respond fast enough to their request for payment for surgery. Vail Valley was willing to negotiate the price all of the way down to $39,500 and Sedera was willing to pay about $36,000 for two levels of necks surgery! However, the surgery was scheduled for Friday, April 18th and they needed the money to be paid immediately. Mike their Needs Coordinator isn''t responding now. They also went to Dr. Lee Nelson who isn''t seeming to recommend surgery. I also gave her Donald Kipp''s number in case that is of interest purely from my own personal experience, not medical advice. She will send me a written email outlining the cost to see if they can get is pre-approved for Sept. or Oct. 2025 instead. I''ll forward to Sedera to see if they will agree.

Also, she had a colonoscopy scheduled for June but now with Redirect ending, I suggested she moves it to May, if possible. Redirect can cover this and then she will enroll in HAB for May 1st start date. She''s fine with the overlap, especially since she needs the colonscopy. She doesn''t want to wait for 6 months and thinks the $4500 will never be sufficient if you include a colonoscopy with the prices they have in Vail. Premium Care will be $603/$1000 + HAB $200 = $803 May 20th billing for June onward.', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2025-04-16 17:06:36', '2025-04-16 17:06:36'),
