  ('zcrm_1579374000162511043', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000162515002', 'Jackson Lawrie', NULL, '4-2-25 Jackson was hired by THIA and is offered benefits starting May 1st. He watched the video and asked good questions. His only health issue is ADHD and he takes a med for it like Adderall. He thinks it''s Buproprion and it looks to be super cheap. He''s a mental health therapist and was on Medicaid. Since he got his new job he just got kicked off Medicaid and has no ins for April. He stopped doing his own mental health visits since he lost Medicaid. He does need visits to get his meds prescribed. He hoping to use virtual health to get that filled. I told him it''s "possible" with the Behavioral Health Specialists," but I can''t be sure. He understood. I offered him HAB since he''d really like to do therapy 1x per week. So, HAB can get him additional benefits beyond Life Care/12 visits and allow him to see his own therapist. He''s happy about that!  He signed up for Secure HSA $1000/$309 paid for by THIA.

He will join 1Dental if THIA pays for it. Cost just increased to $22.95 per month, so I need to get approval first. He will also accept the life ins at $25 max. His mom passed away already and dad is alive. But, he had to go to rehab a few times for alcohol addiction. So, I will run standard rating for Jackson. He doesn''t have any other health issues, so hopefully he''ll meet the Standard rate worst case. he doesn''t know what''s on his record from when in grad school years ago. Zip is 80228 and might move soon. DOB 9/29/96.', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2025-04-02 15:00:58', '2025-04-02 15:00:58'),
