  ('zcrm_1579374000162511001', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000162508012', 'Jessica Smith', NULL, '4-2-25 Jessica is 36 and works for Darrell Porter with Finesse Marketing. She enrolled through their custom site. She lives in Philly, PA so needs Secure HSA. She takes 3 meds that are $2 - $4 each. Methylprednisolone, Naproxen and cyclobezaprine. She has arthritis from a car accident 10 years ago and goes to the ER to get meds for it! I told her Not to do this. First it will be pre-x and not shared and 2nd it will cost 10x more. I recommended starting with the virtual healthcare app and if that''s not possible to go to Urgent Care instead. I told her this will be her responsibility to pay. She''s coming off of government insurance where everything was paid for. Her meds cost nothing either. She listened and understands this will be significantly different than her gov job benefits. She likes the Life Care benefit and the supplement discounts. She''s also traveling to Aruba and knows she''s protected for acute and ER situations while abroad. She also joined 1Dental for dental and vision at the new $22.95 + $30 set up fee. This starts right away, I believe.', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2025-04-02 13:12:41', '2025-04-02 14:40:28'),
