  ('zcrm_1579374000162004107', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000064414873', 'Jillian Livingston', NULL, '3/27/25: Jillian called. She has a colo scheduled on Monday and wants to make sure everything will be good with billing. I double checked the physician - Etemad, Babak, ,M.D. who is in network. She''s having it done at Valley View Hospital and gave me several numbers. I let her know that as long as it''s coded preventive, in network and the hospital sends bill to ARM. She should be good to go. Will call and double check with billing office and reach back out to Jillian when I have solid confirmation. 

Spoke to Lori at ARM and Hospital.
From ARM: it is important to note that the information we have received is that the member had her screening 3 year ago.
Polyps were sent to Pathology, Planstin denied the charges so they were sent to Zion.  I do believe this member will be considered Diagnostic going forward.
When you spoke to the doctor’s office did they offer any of this information?
Do you have access to Zion claims documentation?
The term Screening is important to ARM when processing here.  You didn’t mention it in your email below so maybe this woman is going for diagnostic colo.

Hospital confirmed that Jillian''s PCP ordered a diagnostic colonoscopy. The only way to change that would be for the PCP to send a message to the procedure team letting them know it needs to be a screening. However, this isn''t likely since she''s had a history of polyps. 

