  ('zcrm_1579374000161777253', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000161803002', 'Alison Tomlinson', NULL, '3-21-25 Alison wants to enroll for April 1st. She hit the panic button! She watched all of the videos and was well prepared but didn''t realize that her Cobra is running out end of March. She pulled over while driving to enroll immediately. Alison is 54 and turning 55 in May. She Referred by Kristen Lassalette.  Looking at this for just her and younger son 19 year old. Her oldest son is 22 and works full time @ company that offers ins. She''s paying $300 for oldest son who has diabetes.  Son  Augie goes to CU. She will use the MEC for compliance with CU. She and Augie are super healthy, no meds. She might have to take meds for hormones but should be affordable. Her employer in a small company and will pay her a stipend for her insurance. She also prefers alternative care and acupuncture. She does acupuncture for preventive purposes but realizes that won''t be a shared unless pre-approved and part of a new incident. She''ll just continue paying on her own. She usually needs the follow up ultrasound for mammo. She just did mammo and might get ultrasound done before end of March. She chose Premium HSA $650/$1000 and paid with cc for now. Will update to ACH when her company supplies the checking acct information for next billing. Patti will honor April 1st start date! Alison was eternally grateful!  She''s also helping her 87 year old parents in MN right now and it''s her mom''s 87 B-Day celebration today.', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2025-03-21 14:21:08', '2025-03-21 14:49:31'),
