  ('zcrm_1579374000161718001', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000134180005', 'Lisa Ben-Zeev', NULL, '3-20-25 Lisa says NOT to recommend RMHP. She was quoted $375 but was billed $1600 for an upper and lower GI colonoscopy what they billed at $27K! Now she''s getting billed for $1600. She spent all day trying to fight it. They finally told her that she has 7 co-pays for this one health procedure. OMG! 
 She also now needs mental health counseling now and it''s showing $375 co-pay thru her RMHP mental health plan. I looked it up again for her. BOTH of her parents died about 6 months ago and now she was diagnosed with ulcerative colitis and can only eat a few things every day. So, I explained HAB to her to see if that will help with mental health, dental, gym and mammo since she has dense breasts and may need the follow up ultrasound or MRI. She chose to add it and will use it for those items and her other preventive will use through RMHP and hope to have a better experience. She''s also learned to use GoodRX instead of running it through RMHP bc she has a huge ded of about $4500 for drugs before anything is covered.  She also shared that her pet insurance with Healthy Paws went up to $575 per month until she increased her ded to $1000 and did 70/30 and now it''s $187 for her 12 yr old dog. That''s still insanely expensive!  She currently has Delta Dental with Cobra that''s $39 a month. She has about 5 more months on that and then we can explore other options.', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2025-03-20 14:44:28', '2025-03-20 15:46:07'),
