  ('zcrm_1579374000161676228', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000161676496', 'McKenzie Mann', NULL, '3-20-25 McKenzie came to me via Mindy (Melinda) Grabau. He''s 38 and lives in or near Boulder. He lost service part way through our conversation. He''s an independent contractor. He wants to start as soon as possible. He''s super healthy, no meds, prefers natural, holistic, alternative care. He did get into a car accident in Feb. 2022 and had injury to his vertebrae which he healed with his naturopathic drs. and methods in 4 weeks instead of 8 weeks going down the traditional path. His vm is full. I''ll send him a text.', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2025-03-20 09:20:18', '2025-03-20 09:20:18'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000161675066', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000122117002', 'Leisa Heuple', NULL, '3/20/25: Leisa called saying the surgery center called back and let her know her colo will not be covered. There''s some confusion about whether or not it''s diagnostic and mention that ARM only pays for 1st colo screening (but should be every 5 years). She hasn''t had one in 5 years and claims it is just a preventive screening. We called ARM and LVM for Monica asking her to call me back. Will touch base with Leisa once I learn more. 

Leisa called back - she spoke to her provider who told her that since she''s had polyps in the past, they have to code it diagnostic. I let her know that if they do that, it will not be paid for by MEC. She could submit it as a sharing request and pay the first $1000 or see if provider will code it preventive and if they find something, then code it diagnostic. 

Monica from ARM called and stated the same as provider - that since Leisa had a colo 4 years ago and they found polyps, this isn''t a preventive screening - it''s a check up to check the state of her colon and will be coded diagnostic.AM', 'Concierge', 'Concierge', '2025-03-20 09:13:31', '2025-03-20 09:33:55'),
