  ('zcrm_1579374000161501022', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000131477004', 'Jason Ketcham', NULL, '3-18-25 Isabella and her husband already joined Universal Healthshare Fellowship for about $628 a month and a $5000 IUA. They are part of Secure HSA right now and still have outstanding bills with Zion for the birth of their daughter in the NICU. She was confused by Zion''s notice stating a 1 year waiting period for maternity. She thought it was 1 or 2 years and they don''t want to wait that long in case they choose to have another baby. I let her know they changed it to 6 months and they are grandfathered in already since they joined Feb. of 2024. It''s not relevant to them. I suggested they move to a $2500 IUA to lower their cost to $658 per month on Secure HSA or move to Care+ $2500/$550 and add HAB $250 = $800. That might be too expensive for them. They probably should just stay with SECURE HSA. Maternity will be $2500 at the $2500 IUA level.', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2025-03-18 12:14:19', '2025-03-18 12:14:19'),
