  ('zcrm_1579374000161215001', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000162067003', 'Andrew Somps', NULL, '3-13-25 Andrew is now confused. He spoke with a broker for trad ins who sent him in a whole new direction. He''s proposing an offshoot/subsidiary (?) of UHC for both adults and Select Health for John for a total of $450+$309= $759 with $0 deductibles. But he has no idea the mop for each. Then he could be liable for $8K per family member = $24K vs $3k-$7500 with MCS. Also maternity will cost him much more likely. Also, if he gets a job and wo benefits then his income will change and he will lose his subsidy. If MCS, income doesn''t matter. They are both 33 and John is about 2 I think. They are considering the 6 month wait for maternity CARE+ $2500/$550 or $1000/$672. Also considering no waiting per and choosing Premium Care $1000/$837, $1500/$741 or $2500/$680. He will go back and discuss with his wife.  If gets on unemployment he will likely earn $760 per week which is $39,520. So, the C4 plans actually look super affordable. I left him another vm to tell him to look at the samples I''m sending.', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2025-03-13 09:22:15', '2025-03-13 09:30:14'),
