  ('zcrm_1579374000160427058', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000065203137', 'Sarah Wright', NULL, '02.27.25 - Bob called requesting access to the member portal, provided member ID. Needs to find a new PCP for their son Max. Resent ARM card and gave instructions on how to access network providers. Also requested their 1095 form. JA', 'MPB Health Member Notification', 'MPB Health Member Notification', '2025-02-27 12:06:48', '2025-02-27 12:07:03'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000160428038', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000005173089', 'Diane Forsberg', NULL, 'Diane called stating she never got or saw her digital ARM card that was emailed to her, nor hard copies sent to her as of yet. To which I made sure while on the phone together that she received the email I re-sent her with her digital ARM card, and the details with the link to showing all covered ACA preventative services. As she was wondering what was all that her MEC benefits entailed. I lastly, put a request in the ARM portal for hard copied to be mailed out. Verified her mailing address. -KF', 'Concierge', 'Concierge', '2025-02-27 12:03:03', '2025-02-27 12:03:03'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000160421012', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000159347002', 'Mark Wagoner', NULL, 'Member enrolled &amp; then when filling out the questionnaire in the Sedera Portal re: health questions realized that his spouse might have a Pre-Ex condition.  The have reconsidered enrolling due to no sharing in the 1st year, as a precaution.  I will cancel prior to start and refund all monies collected.', 'Patti Baron', 'Patti Baron', '2025-02-27 12:00:56', '2025-02-27 12:00:56'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000160428033', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000058356101', 'Jonathan Webster', NULL, 'Margaret called in and stated she called and spoke to someone leaving a message but didn''t ever get a call back, so she wants to speak to a real human in her words. She just had questions about what her plan entails coverage wise as far as family counseling for her, her husband, and son. To which I explained that she absolutely has a variety of different types of counseling services included at no extra cost with her plan. I told her in detail how the MSEAP program works in full, with 12 FREE sessions for a whole year, per family member, and broken up into 3 sessions a month, then a 2-month break, back to 3 a month with a 2-month break, etc. Until reaching the 12 sessions in the whole year. I answered her question about there being a network for MSEAP to stay in of Providers/Therapists to see. I answered with yes, she will call MSEAP, verify her MPB.Health plan benefits, and then the MSEAP person will do a provider search in real time over the phone. She lastly asked if her plan has any preventative coverage, as she does not. She said that is fine as she and her family have a separate plan that covers all of preventative. She just wasn''t sure so she knew who to use first for that. I ended off with saying I would put together an email with details on what we discussed about MSEAP, with links & the login code for MSEAP''s website/member portal to see everything included with MSEAP. -KF', 'Concierge', 'Concierge', '2025-02-27 11:58:53', '2025-02-27 11:58:53'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000160427028', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000120892002', 'Carly Swift', NULL, 'Per Carly''s request to find out if CPD or ICD 10 codes are considered preventive. Emailed the response from ARM JA

There is no single CPT or ICD-10 code for annual physicals, per CPT and ICD-10 coding guidelines there are a wide range of codes.  Providers will need to refer to their office billers to determine the services provided and how best to code them.  Primary Care Physicians and OBGYN providers should be aware of preventive care coding, I’ve never seen a preventive visit billed by a Chiropractor before; these providers are considered Specialists.', 'MPB Health Member Notification', 'MPB Health Member Notification', '2025-02-27 11:40:36', '2025-02-27 11:40:36'),
