  ('zcrm_1579374000160211013', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000061006173', 'Brian Delaney', NULL, '2-24-25 Brian was surprised to see his cost go from $386 to $419 + cc fees. So, he''s changing his payment method to ACH. He chose to move from Secure HSA to Premium Care. He never funds an HSA. He only has a healed shoulder and no other pre-x. I explained the new pre-x clause and he understands. I also let him know the price pay increase  a little around June 1st, so he''s prepared for that. He completed the new Zion to Sedera Switch form and chose $1000/$285 for April 1st, onward. All set.', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2025-02-24 16:16:51', '2025-02-24 16:16:51'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000160211008', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000162057106', 'Deland Craven', NULL, '2-24-25 Deland was referred by Heather Bingham. Deland''s DOB 9/9/1965, 80501. He was laid off in Nov. 2023 after working for the same company for 10 years. He''s been living off of severance and his stock buyout. He''s on Cobra now but it''s $1000+ a month for just him! That include dental and vision. He was paying a lot bc he didn''t want to worry about it but now it''s way too much money. He was a creative director at a tech firm and now doing some teaching at Front Range College and piecing together multiple streams of income. Last year he earned $32K and guessing around $50K this year to play it safe. With that he will get a $550 APTC. He take meds for cholesterol, blood pressure and thyroid, all generics and super affordable. The biggest concern for not doing MCS is he has a bi-cuspid valve and aeortic dilation which is genetic and only found accidentally when chose to do a free scan about 10 years ago. No issues but he gets it checked with a cardiogram 1x per year to make sure all is well.  
He watched the video and is intrigued about MCS. He could choose Premium Care and layer on ACA for 1-3 years and still pay way less than $1000+. But, not sure if it makes sense to do MCS too since he''s turning 60 in June and will be heading to Medicare close to when the pre-x clause lifts entirely. He will review the UHC/RMHP and Cigna plans I sent to him to review. He thinks he has a C4 account. I sent him instructions to select me as his agent. Cobra runs out in a few months. He will let me know when he''s ready to proceed. He also wants to keep Dr. Hilary Wallace at BCH. She was in both networks.', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2025-02-24 16:05:50', '2025-02-26 21:36:14'),
