  ('zcrm_1579374000159575003', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000146332002', 'Peter Muerset', NULL, 'We do not supply 1095 A forms. I asked Patti what that form was as I never heard of that one before. After pulling up Peter here, he wouldn''t get either A or C the one we do. Patti asked me to have her call him to get that explained. -KF', 'Concierge', 'Concierge', '2025-02-14 07:23:23', '2025-02-14 07:23:23'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000159532031', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000122624002', 'Keith Damiano Jr.', NULL, '2-13-25 Keith lives in NJ now! So, he needs to keep the MEC. He''s interested in adding his wife (30''s) and 18 month old daughter. This would allow his wife to change jobs potentially and not take the terrible ins they are offering. Keith has Secure HSA and it would be $780/$1000 or $2500/$658.  He''s self-employed. They just moved to NJ 08722. They are considering having another baby. I let him know to make sure she''s not pregnant now or before they join! I read the changes to maternity upcoming for April 1st. If they join before April 1st, they won''t be subject to the 1 year waiting period for maternity.  They are going to figure out what she will be doing for work moving forward. He''s also interested in dental and vision. I sent him 1dental and VSP choices to review. No rush on that front. He''s very happy that we talked and will decide. Meeting tentatively next week.', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2025-02-13 15:41:08', '2025-02-13 15:41:08'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000159532026', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000117297011', 'Piyush Kansara', NULL, '2-13-25 Piyush''s son is 24 and just lost his job and benefits. Job ended on Jan. 22 and benefits ended Jan. 27th. Cobra begins Jan. 28th if he wants Cobra. He''s choosing to join Piyush''s account as a single tax filer. They don''t want Medicaid and added self-employment income of $23K. He doesn''t know what his son will wind up doing for work but he''s not getting unemployment. Their APTC remains the same at $1746.50 and Parth''s is $318.31 and combined it''s $2064.81. He chose to include Parth on their plan. They are keeping their plan and it''s copied above. He''ll be paying about $25 more total for Parth to be on the plan as well. I uploaded the 1st two pages of the Cobra  letter showing the end date. He will also call Cigna to make sure his payment is all set moving forward. He will call in 10 days and added it to his calendar. All set for now!', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2025-02-13 15:05:00', '2025-02-13 15:47:41'),
