  ('zcrm_1579374000159267053', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000175078001', 'Christopher Parsons', NULL, '2-11-25 Chris came to me via David Williams. Chris is a Financial Advisor and is interested for himself and for his clients. He''s 54 and healthy. He did have a partial knee replacement in 2023. So, that''s a pre-x of course. He''s also curious for a client in MA. I let him know that client will need Premium HSA vs what I''m recommending for him which is Premium Care. He''s not taking any meds now. Wants the price sheets for both. He watched my 15 min. interview video and the 9 minute video. He''s not looking for referral money since it''s good for his business. However, he''s happy to accept the $100 as well. Either way, he''s happy. He part of a Financial Advisors Group Health Plan with Vault Medical, Edison and using NBFSA Pharmacy Program. He''s still waiting for the hospital to be paid. The dr. was paid but not the hospital. He got a bill for $24K. The cash price was $24K. But, then they changed it to $62,862 and now billed him for $24K bc nobody has paid yet. There''s also the PHCS network involved and uses the AMPS Advanced Pricing Medical Solutions to make the payments. But, something seems to be amiss with his surgery payment. So, he''s over it and wants to switch. Plus, he''s paying $715 a month with a $2500 ded and $5000 mop. We discussed Premium Care and possibly HAB for about half the price and hopefully much better experience. He thinks April 1st is the earliest start date. He wants his bill to be paid first.', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2025-02-11 21:32:48', '2025-02-11 21:32:48'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000159267048', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000003848025', 'Jennika Wildau', NULL, '2-11-25 Jennika switched from Care+ to Premium Care for March 1st. Her monthly amount is going from $510 to $432. No pre-x other than something she''s had forever that she just pays for on her own. She''s going to let her partner know and let him decide if he wants to join her membership or have his own. They aren''t legally married but live together as domestic partners. I gave her the prices for him separately as well. They will decide by noon on Feb. 19th. She was thrilled at how easy it was to convert with the form. All set!', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2025-02-11 16:52:39', '2025-02-11 16:52:39'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000159267043', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000012223122', 'Elizabeth Daly', NULL, '2-11-25 Elizabeth called to check on Keira''s membership that we are hoping to keep active as of Feb. 1st when she aged out. I haven''t heard back from Sedera. So, I escalated the email and hope to hear back no later than Friday. Elizabeth was thinking of having her husband join Dr. Tusek to have a primary care dr. But, there''s no real need to move then yet. She''s worried about the price increase when she turns 60 in Sept. I told her to hold off until we know what the price increases will be since that would double their IUA''s to be responsible for. They already have Keira moving to her own membership. She''s paying $863 for the family now. It will be $863 + $237 for Keira at the $1000 IUA level.', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2025-02-11 15:57:35', '2025-02-11 15:57:35'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000159267038', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000157910087', 'Lena Wenzel', NULL, '2-11-25 Lena is on https://myplan.ameritas.com/ Vision for $10.67 which is their cheapest plan and allows for lenses and frames every other year and an exam every year. She might want to switch to VSP Choice Plan A for $15.97 if she wants glasses every year instead. She thought she got them every year before but that''s not what her plan shows. She has the Prime Star Select Vision.', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2025-02-11 15:05:21', '2025-02-11 15:05:21'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000159297119', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000143045002', 'Matthew Swasey', NULL, '2/11
Sarah called because she received a bill from pathology from her pap. After reviewing the ARM portal I informed her that the pathology department did not submit that bill. sarah will ask them  to submit the bill to arm and will check up in two weeks to see if it was processed AC', 'Concierge', 'Concierge', '2025-02-11 14:51:58', '2025-02-11 14:51:58'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000159267033', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000155863212', 'Hillary Thomas', NULL, '2-11-25 Tracy called bc HAB denied some labs, allergy treatments, etc. I explained the HAB vs Premium Care for benefits. She''s sort of back on track but will likely need more coaching as they go. Hillary just did $2K worth of labs that she wanted to do. Some will be reimbursed with HAB but others not. She had told me she''s ok with paying some of this stuff. Hopefully that remains true. Tracy will try to reign her in since most of it will not be reimbursed since its far beyond the scope of normal preventive.', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2025-02-11 14:43:56', '2025-02-11 14:43:56'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000159282325', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000156744038', 'David Descoteaux', NULL, '2/11/25: Sent FU email for RX coupons provided last week for Hailey Fe. AM', 'Concierge', 'Concierge', '2025-02-11 14:38:22', '2025-02-11 14:38:22'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000159282315', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000032281037', 'Tammie Petty', NULL, '2/11/25: Tammie called to cancel membership bc she is aging into medicare. Guided her to form online. I see Patti says she''s cancelled Effective 3/25, but Tammie wants to be cancelled effective 3/1 so I advised her to fill out the form just in case. AM', 'Concierge', 'Concierge', '2025-02-11 14:33:44', '2025-02-11 14:33:44'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000159282310', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000142967002', 'Robert Miller', NULL, '2/11/25: Robert called - he''s still having the same issue as before (see note on 1/6) where his PT is billing ARM and refusing to bill him as cash pay even though he''s requested it several times. The difference between Insurance and cash pay is about $500 per visit. On top of that, he''s having to wait a long time for the bills to be "adjusted" by ARM and unsure at this point what he actually owes. I offered to give ARM and the provider office a call - Core Institute 623-537-5615 -- tomorrow morning and see if there''s anything we can do to help his situation. Will follow up with him tomorrow. AM', 'Concierge', 'Concierge', '2025-02-11 14:32:02', '2025-02-11 14:32:02'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000159321025', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000110880002', 'Alexander Crowe', NULL, '02.11.25 Alexander called inquiring about chiropractic care for his wife injury. Advised that he would need to submit the bills to Zion, once the IUA is met. Given that it is related to an injury, he may not need a PCP consult. Alexander will speak with his wife to find out what info she has with the bills, when she received the chiro consults and will get back to us to assist in opening the need with Zion. JA', 'MPB Health Member Notification', 'MPB Health Member Notification', '2025-02-11 14:24:21', '2025-02-11 14:24:21'),
