  ('zcrm_1579374000159176083', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000153961021', 'Patricia Lenz', NULL, '2-10-25 Here are my communications with Patty after she joined on Dec. 6th. She asked more questions about women''s health and here are my answers later on Dec. 6th.

On Fri, Dec 6, 2024 at 8:40 PM wendys mympb.com <wendys@mympb.com> wrote:
Hi Patty,

Here are all of the questions and answers:

Do you reimburse for implantation of an IUD? If so, does it need to be coded in a certain way?  
Not eligible. 

If a client had a preventive mammogram in May or June and was asked to do a follow up MRI due to dense breasts which she never did bc she was going to have to pay for it in full, will Health Access reimburse her for this if she does the MRI in January? She would be a new member as of Jan. 1st, 2025.  
We will not honor the breast MRI or breast ultrasound if we have no record of a screening mammogram in our system. 

If a client does a baseline preventive thermogram instead of a mammogram, will Health Access reimburse for the initial and follow up thermogram say 3-6 months later?
No,  we will only honor the breast thermogram once a year in place of a screening mammogram. 

Many women keep asking me about reimbursements for hormone health visits when dealing with peri menopause or menopause. Are any of these dr. visits or labs reimbursable?
No, they are not reimbursable. 

Sorry, I don''t have better news on these questions. Someday, hopefully this will be different.

Best wishes,


12--8-24

