  ('zcrm_1579374000159049038', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000081878009', 'Linda Pearce', NULL, '02.06.25:  Linda called. Said she doesn''t feel comfortable w/ the Sedera plan because her husband heard they don''t reimburse members for 6 mos., etc. Also, she told them she vapes and they now will be charging her an extra $75/mo. for nicotine use (she says there''s very little nicotine in what she vapes). Furthermore, she learned they will only pay up to $25,000 per need for the following conditions: cancer,  respiratory &vascular disease (including coronary and stroke), oral & esophageal disease and gastric & duodenal ulcers.
She wanted to know if there are any other plan options that would keep her cost down. I explained other IUA options for Premium Care and IUA options for Care+. I told her Zion has similar guidelines for smokers but their monthly smoking fee is $50/mo. and their pay-out limit is $50,000/need but their monthly fees are higher than Sedera.
Linda said she''ll discuss it w/her husband and get back to me either tomorrow or Monday. I will email her pricing for the plans we discussed and both MCS smoking guidelines. JSP', 'Concierge', 'Concierge', '2025-02-07 08:38:57', '2025-02-07 08:38:57'),
