AM', 'Concierge', 'Concierge', '2025-01-29 12:45:29', '2025-01-29 12:45:29'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000158151239', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000059150079', 'Heather Palentchar', NULL, '1/29/25: Heather called in wondering if she could go to a functional med dr for her annual. I explained that it really comes down to the billing. If they are licensed and bill the visit as a wellness check up and part of network, then yes. I resent Heather her ARM email and card. She''s going to check with the provider and ARM. AM', 'Concierge', 'Concierge', '2025-01-29 12:42:21', '2025-01-29 12:42:21'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000158158111', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000001746011', 'Laura Seraydarian', NULL, '1-29-25 I showed Laura two illustrations for Life Ins IUL to illustrate long term retirement income. We did $100 mo. to start which isn''t enough to income to be illustrated. Then we did $125 for yrs 1-2, $250 yrs. 3-4, $500 yrs 5-6 and $1000-$1200 yrs 7-70. Then she can have $38K per year, as loan for life. Page 30 shows this. At age 87 she input $250K and has used $647,870 and has a DB of $244K still available. Therefore, she has about $900K for her $250K investment. She will review her income, debt, expenses and determine what''s comfortable to do. She''s thinking $125 for 2-3 years and then $250 possibly onward. She will let me know. We will build it conservatively with low and high caps.', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2025-01-29 12:36:40', '2025-01-29 12:36:40'),
