  ('zcrm_1579374000158110069', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000002630141', 'Cameron Elmendorf', NULL, '1/28/25: Spoke to Cameron regarding her concerns with Rocky Mountain Cancer Center and not accepting cash pay and needing to find a hematologist or a provider to assist with anemia care. She has very low ferritin and needs high does iron infusions. 
I let Cameron know that in the case of someone being diagnosed with Cancer, and needing to find a treatment facility, we would do a very thorough search in their area, check reviews and quality level, and call them 1 by 1 to make sure the process with member will be smooth. Also, that in my time here, I''ve only ran onto one instance where a provider refused to take a self-pay patient so it isn''t very common at all. 

I let her know I would do the same for the hematologist and get back to her in the next few day with some options. AM', 'Concierge', 'Concierge', '2025-01-28 17:33:07', '2025-01-28 17:33:07'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000158110064', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000133307002', 'Felix Costa', NULL, '1/28/25: Emailed Rosemarie lab quote per request. She sent labs to concierge email. AM', 'Concierge', 'Concierge', '2025-01-28 17:01:47', '2025-01-28 17:01:47'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000158110046', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000133732002', 'Megan Keyser', NULL, '1/28/25: Megan called wanting to know if a series of tests her dr is wanting to do will be covered. I advised her that if the tests are indeed preventive and part of the drs annual checks, and coded as part of her routine wellness checkup AND the provider is in network, then yes, they will be. AM', 'Concierge', 'Concierge', '2025-01-28 16:28:59', '2025-01-28 16:28:59'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000158110038', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000131098002', 'Dana Petty', NULL, '1/28/25: Put in share request January, never heard anything about it. shareable, but pending member action. They''s already paid the deductible with insurance for her shoulder issues. I connected Dana with Zion and verified that yes, they do have to use other insurance first, however I don''t know about paying another $5k deductible for 2025 since the calendar year has started over for the other plan. I also wasn''t certain if Zion would require them to pay an additional IUA since it''s a bilateral injury. Essentially, the daughter has a condition where her shoulders pop out of place. She ended up in the ER last year bc of it (couldn''t get shoulder back in) and the Dr recommended she have surgery on both. Set a follow up for Dana for 2 weeks to check on status and determination from Zion. Seems like this may turn into a sticky situation. AM', 'Concierge', 'Concierge', '2025-01-28 16:07:30', '2025-01-28 16:19:07'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000158110030', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000079839002', 'Richard Goecke', NULL, '1/28/25: Richard called wondering about a 1099 form. I explained what I knew about the "1095" form and provided him with accounting email to get more info. Put his name in teams chat to send 1095. AM', 'Concierge', 'Concierge', '2025-01-28 15:53:18', '2025-01-28 15:56:10'),
