  ('zcrm_1579374000158110020', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000153947018', 'Maritza Galaviz', NULL, '1/28/25: Maritza called wanting to get better prices for prescription. I emailed her RX quote form and let her know we''d get it back to her within 24 hours - most likely by tomorrow morning. AM', 'Concierge', 'Concierge', '2025-01-28 15:42:23', '2025-01-28 15:42:23'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000158110010', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000129873002', 'Daniel Kiefer', NULL, '1/28/25: Daniel LVM about his Cirrus account and getting error message "no records found". Called back and left a very detailed message letting him know that I would put a support ticket into Cirrus for the error he''s getting and reach back out tomorrow after I see it''s resolved. AM', 'Concierge', 'Concierge', '2025-01-28 15:33:38', '2025-01-28 15:33:38'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000158115023', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000059281121', 'Dechen Hawk', NULL, '1/28/2025
Dechen contacted us regarding two bills from August, questioning why ARM is not covering the $289. I explained that during August, he was insured under Planstin, which handles preventative coverage, and that we needed to confirm how the bill was coded.  
We initiated a three-way call with Planstin, where their representative clarified that the provider coded the visit as an office visit rather than preventative. When Dechen stated it was a preventative visit, the Planstin rep advised him to request a recode from the provider.  
On a follow-up call with the provider (with the Planstin rep still on the line), the provider explained that the visit was coded as diagnostic because Dechen requested an Rx refill, disqualifying it as preventative. The Planstin representative stated they could only apply PPO discounts for that visit.  
Additionally, the provider clarified that their policy involves issuing two bills: one for the physician and another for the hospital.  
Dechen expressed frustration, blaming the concierge for not advising him properly, and believes we should be responsible for the bill. I informed him I would escalate the issue to my supervisor for review. Ac', 'Concierge', 'Concierge', '2025-01-28 15:27:52', '2025-01-28 15:27:52'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000158110003', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000133307002', 'Felix Costa', NULL, '1/28/25: Rosemary called back to verify info, she gave me the family''s DOB''s and will call back with ssn &gt; I updated their DOB in Zoho and A123. 
She also has labwork to get a quote on but having trouble uploading to form. I asked her to send them to concierge email and I''d work on them. We also discussed IUAs, submitting bills to Zion. AM', 'Concierge', 'Concierge', '2025-01-28 15:09:04', '2025-01-29 08:30:46'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000158087003', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000027993452', 'Holly Wiese', NULL, '01.28.25 - Holly called at the pharmacy, who was stating that her insurance was not active and she had a $200 co-pay. She was still presenting her Planstin card, states that she never received from MPB with updated information. RE-sent new card for the 3rd time. JA', 'MPB Health Member Notification', 'MPB Health Member Notification', '2025-01-28 14:30:51', '2025-01-28 14:30:51'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000158083003', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000092115002', 'Nicolas Gossum', NULL, '01.28.25 - Member requested his receipt, emailed. Opened IT ticket to ensure it sends out automatically in the future. JA', 'MPB Health Member Notification', 'MPB Health Member Notification', '2025-01-28 14:00:11', '2025-01-28 14:00:11'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000158079008', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000002630141', 'Cameron Elmendorf', NULL, '1-28-25 Cam is concerned bc Rocky Mountain Cancer Center won''t accept self pay patients at all!  She tried calling and asking multiple different people and they all give her a hard No. I even see MPowering, Secure Care, Zion and Sedera on their site as memberships they won''t accept. I sent a note asking our Concierge Team and Julia responded with this, "Hi Wendy, I''ve heard of a few cases where cash pay is not accepted. I do not think we have around this on our end, since it is at the discretion of the practice/doctor. Is there another provider in the area? We can assist in the search and appointment scheduling if needed."  There''s not much more I can do. She''s concerned for future, not for any current problem. Trad ins will still be way more limited for most everything else. She would have to use a different provider if she were to ever have a cancer diagnosis. That is NOT her problem. She just has anemia and needs an infusion.', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2025-01-28 13:55:43', '2025-01-28 13:55:43'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000158079003', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000046294057', 'Holly Goldstein', NULL, '1-28-25 Holly called bc her Planstin card was rejected. She didn''t know of the new ARM card. I told her to call the Concierge Team for help with a colonoscopy she wants to get soon and to obtain the newest version of the card and network, etc.', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2025-01-28 13:51:27', '2025-01-28 13:51:27'),
