  ('zcrm_1579374000157962179', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000148561005', 'Michelle Tani', NULL, '01.27.2025 Michelle called to confirm about her taxes and the membership she has with us. I kindly explained that her membership with us is purely for emergencies/large medical bills. She did share that she has preventive insurance through an outside entity, and will contact them regarding any tax paperwork. NT', 'Concierge', 'Concierge', '2025-01-27 16:15:14', '2025-01-27 16:15:14'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000157962163', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000158795002', 'Deatra Jones-Dixon', NULL, '1-27-25 Deatra is 27 turning 28 in Feb. She works for Julie Oldham. Julie will pay for her plan as a reimbursement. Deatra doesn''t have any health ins at the moment. She''s healthy, no pre-x, no meds, no tobacco. She doesn''t do that annual wellness visits and didn''t recall Julie mentioning an additional wellness benefit. She will inquire. I described Premium Care $1000 IUA / $237 and $125/$25 for March 1st start date. She makes about $80K, so not good candidate for ACA at her age.', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2025-01-27 15:55:15', '2025-01-27 15:55:15'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000157962152', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000129823144', 'Pam Adamson', NULL, '1-27-25 Pam wants to remove Darryl from her membership bc he gets Cobra now for one more month. But, I just realized it''s past the deadline to make changes. So, I told her to call me back.', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2025-01-27 15:43:16', '2025-01-27 15:43:16'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000157962144', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000012051083', 'Nancy Gentry', NULL, '1-27-25 Nancy called me and I told her to call the Concierge to get her new ARM card since Planstin is disabled. It looks like she already called the Concierge anyhow. Looks like she''s all set.', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2025-01-27 15:30:08', '2025-01-27 15:30:08'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000157962130', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000138597002', 'Bladimir Aviles', NULL, '1-27-25 Bladimir completed the change form to add MEC, ie. moving from Care+ to Secure HSA for March 1st onward. He will be all set with a 63 day allowance for no MEC in MA. He had an open Need to he dealt with and Zion gave him a debit card to pay for the expenses above his $1000 IUA. They didn''t find any issues, so it''s not necessarily resolved. I let him know if he has any more visits related to this same health issue to submit it immediately, so they will hopefully keep it all in the one current open need. I let him know if he''s symptom, treatment and diagnosis free for 12 months it will definitely become a new Need and he''ll have to pay $1000 again at that time. 
I also sent him the HSA information to set up his own HSA account to get the tax benefits for 2025. 
He was on Mass Health for Jan. - May of 2024. I let him know to contact Mass Health for the tax form for that part of the year. We don''t have a form for Jun - Dec. He will be all set for 2025 since added the MEC for March 1st onward. He''s allowed a 63 day lapse in MA.  His monthly savings likely exceed the amount to pay full cost through Mass Health. He said he didn''t qualify for APTC when he looked into it in 2024 after his divorce that was official in Aug. 2024. His accounting, income and SEP may take affect Aug. or within 60 days. Any adjustment on taxes may just cancel out due to the savings he had from choosing CARE+ vs Secure HSA, since he didn''t need or want ACA compliant screenings.  
https://www.mass.gov/technical-information-release/tir-24-1-individual-mandate-penalties-for-tax-year-2024#_ftn3', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2025-01-27 15:19:18', '2025-01-27 15:27:20'),
