  ('zcrm_1579374000157962100', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000163576188', 'Daniel McCarthy', NULL, '1-27-25  Wendy - I have the Rocky Mountain Health Plan Valley Colorado Option Gold plan thru Connect for Health Colorado and you are my broker. 

I have been having some eye issues and have been seeing a Retinal Ophthalmologist in Grand Junction.  Yesterday, after a thorough exam, he diagnosed that I have a rare issue that requires surgery.  He said he does not do this specialized surgery and said only about a dozen ophthalmologist in the US do the procedure and that none are in Colorado.  

It has been very stressful to be told I need a rare/specialized surgical procedure.  Adding to my stress is not knowing if my health insurance will pay for an out of state surgical procedure.  What is the process to confirm my health insurance will pay for this out of state procedure?  

Please call or email me at your earliest convenience.  Thanks.  

Dan McCarthy
313-805-3864

____________

I spoke with Dan and he will call RMHP and see if they will pre-approve the eye surgery out of state since there''s nobody in the state of CO who performs these surgeries. He lives in GJ. He will work on this. I told him they might, in rare cases, allow for Continuity of Care when there''s nobody who will carry out the procedure in state.', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2025-01-27 12:32:12', '2025-01-27 12:46:44'),
