I guided Alyssa to use the healthcare.gov to make sure she can request a service that is in her membership, to separate items that are not covered (as a cash pay service), to allow us to search for savings for labs outside of the ACA, and to call Planstin if she wants information of her history of preventive visits or what they processed. As for ARM, she has not used their services yet. NT', 'Concierge', 'Concierge', '2025-01-24 16:28:53', '2025-01-24 16:28:53'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000157844011', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000100861002', 'Erin Dreistadt', NULL, '01.24.2025 Erin called for membership education. We went over ARM preventive details, I checked if the doctor overlooking the PA she usually goes to see, is in the network: PHCS-Specific Services (AO Today, and per Catherine''s message on Teams chat - Sales-Concierge). I sent her a provider search for Gloria Oberbeck.
I sent her the preventive services email as well, and went over lab-works process and how to conduct her preventive appointments vs cash pay visits.
We discussed the ARM letter and page 3 that says copay visits vs the IUA with Zion.
