  ('zcrm_1579374000157634172', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000001746009', 'Jill Bryant', NULL, '01.23.2025 Missed call from Jill. Returned her call and LVM. 
************************************************************************
Jill called back. We discussed ARM and preventive services. I sent her the preventive email. We also discussed, how large medical bills are handled via Zion, sharing requests, and aging out. 
I pulled up the guidelines and read out loud to her the aging out part
"Aging Out at 65: Medical incidents, services, and expenses that occur prior to the members age-out at sixtyfive (65), will have up to thirty (30) days after their membership end date to submit a sharing request. All other time limits will remain in effect including:
- itemized bills and statements must be submitted within six (6) months of the date of
service, and
- the IUA must be paid within six (6) months of the initial date of service, or they become
ineligible for sharing."

I shared that with the team via Teams Chat to confirm if MPB guidelines on aging out is parallel with Zion''s. Will reach back out to Jill via email or text to confirm with her.  
****************************************************************
Patti responded to my inquiry on Teams Chat. I forwarded the information to Jill via GoTo text. NT', 'Concierge', 'Concierge', '2025-01-23 15:35:38', '2025-01-23 17:56:27'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000157638206', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000015647172', 'Julie Perington', NULL, '1/23
followup email sent AC
Here’s the email template for informing the member about the MRI and offering an alternative option:  

---

**Subject:** Follow-Up on Your MRI Appointment  

Dear [Member''s Name],  

I hope this message finds you well. I wanted to follow up regarding your MRI. Unfortunately, I’ve confirmed that your MRI will not be covered under your current plan.  

With that being said, I’d like to share an alternative option that may help reduce the cost of the procedure. You can book your MRI through **Radiology Assist**, a platform that offers significantly discounted imaging appointments.  

Here’s how you can proceed:  

1. **Visit the Radiology Assist Website**:  
   Use this link to explore available options: [https://radiologyassist.com/ra-search-results/](https://radiologyassist.com/ra-search-results/).  

2. **Call Radiology Assist for Assistance**:  
   Once you’ve identified a suitable option, you can contact their team directly, and they’ll help you book your appointment.  

 understand this may not be the outcome you were hoping for, but I hope this alternative option makes the process a bit easier for you. If you have any additional questions or need further assistance, please don’t hesitate to reach out.', 'Concierge', 'Concierge', '2025-01-23 15:32:07', '2025-01-23 15:32:07'),
