  ('zcrm_1579374000157634036', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000001637159', 'Gretchen Wegner', NULL, '1-23-25 Gretchen sent me a very nice note. However, if she''s not already enrolled, she may not be able to join Covered CA now without a Life Change Event.

Thanks Wendy! I don''t think there''s anything specific you can help with, and I''m in meetings all morning. My business is in a bit of a freefall right now, and I simply can''t afford the current plan (I paid myself only $40k this year, which is not much at all given I live in the Bay Area of California). So the jump from $295 to $419 PLUS the $345ish that I put into my HSA is simply too much for my pocketbook. 

Here is more explanation that I also put in my form that I just filled out: 

As a perimenopausal woman with a TON of brain fog, I"m finding the need to track all my own healthcare needs, submit everything as a need, etc to be too many executive function tasks. I''d rather be in a system that tracks all my needs centrally, so that I don''t have to be my own "admin". I''m going to explore what a high deductible insurance plan at Kaiser Permanente looks like, and if I discover after a year that the healthshare plan is better, I''ll shift back.

Also, as a self-employed S-Corp, I''ve learned there are additional tax benefits for providing insurance for myself as an employee that I don''t seem to be able to get with the healthshare plan, so it just makes sense to explore this this year (my lowest earning year ever!).

The problem with the healthshare plan is that when I use it regularly (when I have a need) I remember how it all works, and then if I don''t use it for several months, I forget how it works. the stress of having to remind myself what needs can be submitted, how to submit needs, etc, is just too much as my brain is losing capacity from perimenopause. What I like about Kaiser Permanente is all my health needs will be in one system that THEY Can track, thus (hopefully) sparing my cognitive overload from being my own admin.

I do want to reiterate that I''ve very much appreciated the health share plan! It served an important need for me over the last many years and I so appreciate it deeply. It''s also taught me how to advocate for myself with doctors, and I never even KNEW about HSA''s until i was required to get one by mpowering benefits. So I''m very satisfied... and might come back. But for now, especially given the tax savings because of the tax structure of my business, it makes sense to shift.', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2025-01-23 11:38:29', '2025-01-23 11:38:29'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000157638023', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000156744038', 'David Descoteaux', NULL, 'Both her Gyno provider and the Derm facility are in the network for ARM with Practitioner/Ancillary services! Yay, will give a call back to let Julia know and how to move forward. -KF', 'Concierge', 'Concierge', '2025-01-23 11:36:55', '2025-01-23 11:36:55'),
