  ('zcrm_1579374000157532065', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000134444002', 'Bonnie Nkrumah', NULL, '01.22.2025 Emailed Bonnie my finding from the results on the 20th. Email is in the concierge/crm email. Closed the task. NT', 'Concierge', 'Concierge', '2025-01-22 16:56:09', '2025-01-22 16:57:47'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000157532052', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000064414873', 'Jillian Livingston', NULL, '01.22.2025 Emailed Jillian Sherry Myer''s response regarding Axel''s therapist, Andrea Kulbert. The email can be found in the concierge email. Sherry''s response "Hi Nahla, Thanks for reaching out! We brought on Andrea Kulbert last summer. She is in our provider network. We can approve 12 sessions for Axel for the year, that he can use in a row without taking a break. Please have Jillian contact us directly to confirm she would like an authorization sent out for Axel and we will get right on that. You can have her ask for me, since I am aware of the situation. However, if I’m unavailable, anyone she speaks to will be able to help her, as well....." NT', 'Concierge', 'Concierge', '2025-01-22 16:47:19', '2025-01-22 16:47:19'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000157532041', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000017243070', 'Felicia Balderston', NULL, '01.22.2025 Felicia went to a gyno visit in 9/12, preventive woman wellness visit code 99386 (preventive visit) but Planstin did not receive that claim. It is now past the 90 day rule, and is no longer the patient''s responsibility. It does not look like Planstin received it, and the provider needs to write it off, unless they can prove that they sent the claim. 
Felicia shared she has been trying to reach Planstin right before calling us, but she could not reach them.  
She also had a  Mammogram 9/03 but shows that it is "pending insurance", Caitlyn shared they received labs that totaled $1611 due to non ACA items on there, and got reduced to $425.95. Caitlyn offered to have a 3way call with Felicia and the OBGYN provider, since they did not bill them, they past that 90 day rule, and the imaging place to make sure they billed the mammogram. 
Follow up with Felicia on her experience with Caitlyn at Planstin.
Felicia will call us back if she needs additional guidance. NT', 'Concierge', 'Concierge', '2025-01-22 16:15:33', '2025-01-22 16:51:10'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000157520073', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000098254002', 'Angela McGuire', NULL, '1/22/25: Spoke to Angela regarding colo appt. and forwarded her medical info to Lalitha at Summit Digestive. Summit urged Angela to call herself in order to finish setting up the appointment and go over more detailed medical information. I provided Angela with their phone number and told her to reach out to us if she runs into any more issues. AM', 'Concierge', 'Concierge', '2025-01-22 15:52:51', '2025-01-22 15:52:51'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000157520068', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000146983002', 'Katherine ann DUERKSEN', NULL, '1/22/25: Spoke to Sedera regarding Katherine''s colonoscopy request. According to them, since Katherine is 40, it would be considered diagnostic regardless. Same with MEC.
Called Katherine to ask her what her deductible is with the marketplace plan to see how that would compare to her $1500 IUA. 
Was also going to recommend that if she ended up using Sedera to pay for the procedure to take advantage of their resources for price negotiation. She can access those by logging into her member portal, selecting "member resources", "features", then "medical concierge" - They can get results in 2-7 business days. 
Left a voicemail for her to call back. If she does - please ask the above questions. AM', 'Concierge', 'Concierge', '2025-01-22 15:49:18', '2025-01-22 15:49:18'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000157532036', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000139351002', 'Debra Rankin', NULL, '01.22.2025 Sent Debra her MRI request results via CRM email. NT', 'Concierge', 'Concierge', '2025-01-22 15:47:10', '2025-01-22 15:47:10'),
