  ('zcrm_1579374000157405018', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000065038052', 'Brian Walsh', NULL, '01.21.2025 Brian called asking what his options were to get his Covid shot. He said he went to CVS and Walgreens, presented his Planstin card, which of course did not work. He said CVS wanted to charge over $500, and Walgreens over $200. I proceeded to try to explain the change in MEC, he cut me off to let me know that he is aware of the change. I assume HE JUST learned that, given he presented his Planstin card. He did call Planstin, and they told him that he no longer has Planstin, but I do not know what else they shared with him.
I shared with him with the new MEC, he will need to go to any other pharmacy, other than CVS and Walgreens, as they are not contracted with Citizens RX - info on the back of his card.
I then moved into helping him find the email we sent to him, with his virtual ARM card. He found a welcome letter from ARM, in the process, then he found the ARM card email we sent, and while he was looking for that one, I sent him the Preventive resources template via CRM.
I attempted to offer him the options on how to get his Covid shot, but he was not being receptive, and kept getting confused. He kept using the word provider, and I addressed that later in the conversation, by changing the angle of pharmacy/Citizens RX, to going to a preventive appt and getting shots that way. 
