  ('zcrm_1579374000157280144', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000151449002', 'Betsy Todd', NULL, '1/20/25: Email Communication with Betsy regarding appts:
Betsy:While I await the sharing request I need your help to make sure I know what to do for my (2) appointments this week:
 I am scheduled to see my doctor as a follow up preventative visit for a breast exam. I still HAVE NOT received my insurance cards via mail. How do I pay for this appointment and properly code it?
 I need to pre register for a breast MRI I am having this week. They do not see "MPB" as a provider that they accept. How do I register and pay for this MRI?

Reply:Hi Betsy,
Here’s how to move forward with your 2 appointments:
Doctor’s Preventative Follow-Up Visit
You can use your digital Preventive MEC card, which was emailed to you, for this visit. However, I recommend reading through the MEC welcome letter to confirm that this specific appointment qualifies as a covered preventive wellness service.
If you have questions about coverage, you may want to call ARM directly at 800-392-1770 to verify before your appointment. Be sure to bring the digital card or a printed version with you to the visit and confirm that the appointment is billed as a preventative wellness visit.
Breast MRI Pre-Registration
Since MRIs are diagnostic, you will need to register as a self-pay patient for this appointment.
I’m assuming this is part of the sharing request you opened. If so after you’ve met your IUA of $1,000 – bills related to this issue can be submitted in your Zion member portal for sharing.
I apologize for the delay in receiving your physical ARM card. ARM is closed today, but you or I can contact them during business hours to check the mailing status.
Let me know if you need further assistance or clarification.
AM', 'Concierge', 'Concierge', '2025-01-20 14:32:59', '2025-01-20 14:32:59'),
