  ('zcrm_1579374000157169011', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000130567002', 'Savannah Lewis', NULL, '1/17/25: Sent a message in mine, Wendy and Savannah''s email thread to make sure Savannah was aware of Zion''s policy around withdrawing from membership when there is an open need: AM

Good morning Savannah and Wendy,
 I just wanted to touch base with you guys about Zion’s policy around how they manage sharing requests when a member cancels.
 According to Chris at Zion, when a member has an open sharing request and withdraws, these things must be true for continued processing of request:
The sharing request is determined eligible
Proof in portal that IUA has been paid
All bills for sharing request submitted prior to becoming inactive
 Savannah, I understand that you’ve already submitted your cancellation request which will be processed by us on the 20th. If Trevor has more bills he needs to submit for this or if any information is missing according to Zion, I would highly recommend staying active at least for another month.
 Ultimately, it is up to you. I just want to make sure you have all the information about how it will affect your open need.
 Kindly,
Angee

Savannah''s response to this was:
I am an insurance agent, and I will not!
 
I had coverage during the time of my bills needing to be paid for by ZION. I have documentation of each time I have called in and who I spoke to. I have done everything by the book. IWILL NOT PAY ANOTHER $500.
 
They cannot decline just because I cancelled at the end of my term due to unsatisfied customer service and the runaround. I will report this if this is what you are hearing.', 'Concierge', 'Concierge', '2025-01-17 09:14:26', '2025-01-17 09:32:31'),
