  ('zcrm_1579374000156923038', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000156930001', 'Vicky Stevens-Lewis', NULL, 'Member submitted Change Form to raise her IUA to $1500 based on something she read about requiring a minimum of a $1500 deductible.  Explained the $3000 deductible associated with the MEC and she was happy to hear that.  I also directed her to go to IRS.gov to look at the list of eligable expenses that HSA $ could be spent on.  She will be staying w/$1000 IUA', 'Patti Baron', 'Patti Baron', '2025-01-15 10:20:28', '2025-01-15 10:20:28'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000156942003', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000157240002', 'Zachary Lovell', NULL, '1-15-25 Zach was Bev''s client. He''s 32 and lives in the Denver area. He wanted to change his income from $58K-$60K to $45K for 2025. However, he proceeded to ask about options that work out of state such as in CA and other places where he spends a large chunk of time. I asked if he had heard of MCS. He and Bev talked about it in the past and he had a decent understanding just not confident in its success. I shared my experience with it. I discussed Premium Care since he might prefer the $1500 IUA to help bring the cost down. Quoted $285/$1000 and $254/$1500 plus $125/$25. He''s fine with doing his annual wellness visit cash pay and not reimbursed since that''s not included. He''s not old enough for a colonoscopy. He has no pre-x, no tobacco, no meds. He''s really looking for protection for acute trauma/accidents. He also has an accident policy to be extra protected. He had to walk into a work meeting. We will revisit at 5:10 this evening to complete the application.', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2025-01-15 10:11:37', '2025-01-15 10:11:37'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000156891070', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000098254002', 'Angela McGuire', NULL, '1/15/25: Performed an extensive search over the past few days trying to verify a place the member can get a routine colonoscopy. To do this, I called a handful of physicians listed as in-network to ask their hospital affiliations for facility where the procedure would be held. Then reached out to hospitals to make sure they accepted what ARM pays which is 150% of the medicare allowable rate. Out of the following hospitals:  Sinai Hospital, Humboldt Park Surgery Center, Swedish Hospital, Rush University, Saint Mary - I was only able to speak to 1 billing dept and they couldn''t give me a solid answer. Left messages and requested call backs from the rest. 

Julia: "I spoke to Lori regarding the issues of Colonoscopies and the 150% Medicare allowable. 
 She had to escalate this issue to Dave Shaul and John Mitchell as they are the ones who make the decisions regarding the financial distribution of their available/collected funds. We should have an answer this week if they can increase the % paid or go to a PPO. 
 We should have answer hopefully this week. In the meantime, please let members know that the MEC vendor is in the process of negotiating with facilities. We should have more info this week."

AM', 'Concierge', 'Concierge', '2025-01-15 10:06:09', '2025-01-15 10:06:09'),
