  ('zcrm_1579374000156747096', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000115751002', 'Rocio Borzage', 'Zion Sharing Request...', '01.14.2025 William called regarding his daughter''s injured ankle. Wanting to learned the best way to proceed to save and help save money. He was told that xrays  are covered by ARM. I read from the Welcome Letter in our resource library, that there is  $50 copay AFTER appeasing the high deductible amount of $5k. He then wanted to know if it is better to have ARM run the bill THEN share it with Zion, or present cash pay, THEN share it with Zion. I explained, given my past experience, ARM would not know off the top of their mind HOW MUCH the bill will become if processed, they need to see the NPI# and other coding. Plus, I shared once presented as a cash pay patient, the cost decreases significantly. 
He asked if we could do a 3way call with ARM, I tried, but they were out to lunch. He said he will call them separately. I will start a task. NT', 'Concierge', 'Concierge', '2025-01-14 12:04:47', '2025-01-14 12:25:28'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000156844064', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000152394019', 'Chad Daigle', NULL, 'Member has already submitted a blank change form to change his IUA.  Per Leo he wants to change to $5000.  I will process.', 'Patti Baron', 'Patti Baron', '2025-01-14 11:48:36', '2025-01-14 11:48:36'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000156738225', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000098610002', 'Kurt Wenrich', NULL, '1/14/25: Cheryl called. Kurt is scheduled to have a colo and the facility told them they don''t have surgical benefits with their plan. I explained that the surgical procedure is paid for through the plan, but the facility fee is paid at a different rate bc there are no hospital benefits through ARM - they are paid at 150% of Medicare rates. 

Lori from ARM offered the following: (in concierge email, Subject: Wenrich)
"Hi Angee, we have confirmed that a Single Case Agreement for this member will be offered.  I spoke with Cheryl Wenrich and suggested her husband keep his appt.
Hopefully, this won’t happen too often going forward."
AM', 'Concierge', 'Concierge', '2025-01-14 11:30:09', '2025-01-14 12:51:50'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000156747077', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000061924134', 'Kristen Lassalette', NULL, '01.14.2025 Kristen Lassalette called, following up on our last conversation regarding the provider billing/not billing, the provider claiming that "THEY SPOKE WITH Planstin, and Planstin shared that they are not an insurance..." - according to Kristen''s experience with the provider. 
PRESENTLY, they are sending her threatening letters regarding billing - Primary Care Provider. Billed Preventive - it shows in their system - the way Caitlyn sees it in her system is Office Visit NOT PREVENTIVE. 
Caitlyn offered to do a 3way call with them at 970-544-7377. Caitlyn called them, while we were on hold....she brought in Rachel from the provider''s office - DOS for PCP - new patient visit - Rachel confirms the way it was coded is Office Visit. Order needs to be corrected to be rebilled - 
Kristen asked Rachel, what does she need to do to - Rachel needs to make that phone call as the patient - coding needs to be corrected for the claim to be corrected and sent properly to Planstin. NT', 'Concierge', 'Concierge', '2025-01-14 11:18:45', '2025-01-14 11:40:04'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000156738220', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000094942002', 'Tim Ottmann', NULL, '1/14/25: Called Tim back. He had questions about ARM card. Let him know it was in his email and physical one will be coming in the mail. I said if he doesn''t get the physical one by end of week, to give us a call and we can check on it for him. AM', 'Concierge', 'Concierge', '2025-01-14 11:16:08', '2025-01-14 11:16:08'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000156850008', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000152394019', 'Chad Daigle', NULL, 'Member Only $1000 IUA Care+. -KF', 'Concierge', 'Concierge', '2025-01-14 11:14:20', '2025-01-14 11:14:20'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000156845073', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000155884002', 'Mark Kitts', NULL, 'No response. Left a detailed message on vm. Sent email to reschedule welcome call after start date of February 1, 2025. Vanessa Orozco', 'Concierge', 'Concierge', '2025-01-14 11:01:34', '2025-01-14 11:01:34'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000156747063', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000148499180', 'Deanna Sais', 'POTENTIAL Zion Sharing Request....', '01.14.2025 Ryan, Deanna''s husband, called from the hospital, where Deanna had an open heart surgery and is in ICU.
Ryan''s initial request for assistance was to learn how to address/present to the billing department, who he claims comes into the room 4-5 times, asking for information on insurance. I explained to Ryan, at first that I''d like to make it easier for him and I to speak more freely, but he''s not on membership. So I will send Deanna a form that won''t take more than 20 seconds or so to fill out. He responded with the fact that Deanna, unfortunately is not in a state that she can do that. With that, I proceeded to offer him extra guidance, and although there''s no signed form, I wanted to offer at least billing procedures and how to present:
"Present as a cash pay patient" - "Collect any itemized bills" - "Later on we can upload all the documents onto Zion''s portal..."
Called Zion to learn of options to help Ryan, if indeed she is incapacitated, how can we bring him on to help with the process.
I go to speak to Isabella from Zion, she put me on hold to get some answers. Here are a few bullets she offered to help, given that Zion needs that PHI from Deanna, but she is not in a state to complete or retrieve it (from what I understood from Ryan).
1- Isabella offered to call Ryan on his phone: (720) 481-6860 
2- Isabella offered to send the PHI form in hopes that maybe he can retrieve it
3- Isabella informed me and will inform Ryan that cases like this will be sent to the EXTENDED CARE TEAM.

I''ve created a task to follow up with Ryan, to see how he and Deanna are doing. NT', 'Concierge', 'Concierge', '2025-01-14 10:57:54', '2025-01-14 12:24:06'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000156738215', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000098254002', 'Angela McGuire', NULL, '1/14/25: Spoke to Monica at ARM about checking eligibility for a facility for Angela''s screening colonoscopy. We went over again that there are no facilities within the network and facility fees are paid at 150% of medicare rates. She offered to send a list of gastroenterologists that I could check the hospital affiliations with. Reached out to Angela and lvm letting her know I was still working on this and should have her something within the next few days. AM', 'Concierge', 'Concierge', '2025-01-14 10:49:26', '2025-01-14 10:49:26'),
