Jen called regarding questions about the phcs. i explained to her that her mec is stricrly preventative no spcialist. shes under the impresion she can go to a specialsit and pay a 30 dollar copay. itold  that ther are no copays and the anything difnoostic she would be finaicaly responisble for Ac', 'Concierge', 'Concierge', '2025-01-14 09:22:20', '2025-01-14 09:22:20'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000156747036', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000011610208', 'Marc Krawatsky', NULL, '01.14.2025 Hillary called to learn if colorgaurd would be covered. In the past with Planstin, we learned that it is covered, but would be considered THE ONCE/Year PREVENTIVE Colon ACA service. Hillary also wanted to know about the timeline restrictions of getting them (every how many years).
I wanted to double check with ARM to see if they are the similar. I spoke with ARM, and the answer is that the members can get both, HOWEVER, the PRIMARY CODING needs to be imperative. It must be PREVENTATIVE.
Also, regarding the timeframe of getting this routine screening depends on the patient: 3, 5 sometimes 10. The representative shared, if the patient is getting the screening so early (3 years in as Hillary shared), gastro challenges might be present or overcome in the past. I''m sharing this part to make sure it matches Hillary''s medical history, and to make sure it is PRIMARILY CODED Preventive. I texted the above to Hillary via GoTo Texting. NT', 'Concierge', 'Concierge', '2025-01-14 08:53:44', '2025-01-14 08:53:44'),
